diff --git a/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsGeometry/doc/master_integration.md b/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsGeometry/doc/master_integration.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..83413687
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsGeometry/doc/master_integration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Rotated geometry on official master
+
+This branch merges `faser/calypso:master` at
+`7f2d16812070a263210d2b2dc56633345e5a10b1` (13 November 2026) into the
+rotation history at `88c457c1`, including the isolated smoothing repair
+`1c06c7b6` and its regression test. The merge retains both parent histories;
+it is not a squash or a replacement of the master source tree.
+
+The new master Tracking package layout is retained. Rotation changes in the
+trajectory state writer and truth parameter tool follow the files to
+`RootWriterTools` and `TrackFinders`. The KalmanFitterTool include conflict
+retains the rotation geometry context and the new `ActsInterop/IndexSourceLink.h`.
+
+The ACTS internal global frame is `(x_A,y_A,z_A)=(z_F,y_F,-x_F)`.
+The default reconstruction material map is packaged as
+`FaserActsGeometry/material-maps-alma9-rotated-rowmajor.json.gz`. It is the
+validated row-major rotation of the alma9 map, preserving geometry IDs,
+binning and material cells. `rotatedMaterialMapPath()` locates the installed
+data through PathResolver, expands it once in a temporary directory, and
+keeps it alive until process exit. No user home path is required.
+
+CKF2 defaults to `IsolateCandidateSmoothing=True`. Each selected candidate
+owns its states before its RTS smoothing runs. The existing test checks
+shared state contamination and private smoothing order independence.
+
+All waveform reconstruction and waveform conditions source is exactly the
+official master version, including `IntegralOneDim`, fit constraints and
+failure fallback. This is distinct from the older waveform implementation
+in the original rotation branch. The original research worktree is retained;
+optional truth position, audit and interface control experiments are not
+enabled or silently copied into this production integration.
+
+The optional `NtupleDumperAlg.RotatedPhysicalAngles` control is retained from
+the validated research worktree, with its existing default. Compact physics
+comparison explicitly converts track momentum and fitted states to the FASER
+frame. The comparison therefore does not interpret ACTS polar angles as
+physical beam angles.
+
+Validation and performance measurements are recorded in the companion
+`nu_muAnalysis` repository, `workbook/stage208_master_integration/`. A build
+alone is not a physics validation: reconstruction must verify the effective
+material bytes, all four isolated smoothing defaults, common truth IDs,
+station momentum response, purity, efficiency and duplicate rates.
