diff --git a/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsKalmanFilter/doc/candidate_smoothing.md b/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsKalmanFilter/doc/candidate_smoothing.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d2b79969
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Tracking/Acts/FaserActsKalmanFilter/doc/candidate_smoothing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Candidate-isolated smoothing in CKF2
+
+`CKF2.IsolateCandidateSmoothing` defaults to `True`. No Python configuration
+change is required to enable it.
+
+The CKF can return several candidates whose state paths share ancestors in an
+ACTS `VectorMultiTrajectory`. The gain-matrix smoother writes its result into
+each visited state's smoothed parameter and covariance buffers. Smoothing a
+later branch can therefore overwrite an earlier branch's shared ancestors.
+Deep-copying the candidates after the finder returns also copies these
+overwritten values.
+
+After candidate selection, CKF2 deep-copies the selected candidate's entire
+state path with `copyFrom(..., true)`, then reruns `Acts::GainMatrixSmoother` on
+that private path. Downstream track conversion, refitting and state writers
+receive candidate-specific smoothed parameters and covariance. A smoothing
+error fails the event rather than exporting partially recomputed states.
+
+The repair leaves candidate ranking, hit selection, predicted/filtered states,
+seed covariance and the CKF's reference-surface fitted parameters unchanged.
+It does not replace the subsequent Kalman refit or modify the ACTS library.
+It recomputes smoothing only for selected candidates, reusing the existing
+deep copy, with work linear in their total number of states.
+
+For a controlled comparison with the previous shared-state output, explicitly
+set `IsolateCandidateSmoothing=False` in the arguments to `CKF2Cfg`, or on the
+configured CKF2 algorithm. This option should be recorded with the results.
+
+The `CandidateIsolatedSmoothing` CTest uses the actual ACTS containers and
+gain-matrix smoother. It reproduces shared-ancestor parameter and covariance
+overwrites, checks the analytical RTS solution after isolation, tests both
+candidate orders, verifies unchanged filtering inputs and reference parameters,
+and checks the single-state endpoint case. Run it after configuring/building
+Calypso in the usual Athena environment:
+
+```sh
+cmake --build build --target FaserActsKalmanFilter_CandidateIsolatedSmoothing --parallel 2
+ctest --test-dir build -R FaserActsKalmanFilter_CandidateIsolatedSmoothing --output-on-failure --no-tests=error
+```
+
+Validated with Athena 24.0.41 (`x86_64-el9-gcc13-opt`): the package CTest passes.
+A real Calypso smoke run uses DSID 110051, the first RDO file's entries [0,20),
+rotated geometry and unchanged seed/selection settings. Its 42 writer tracks
+contain 718 measurement states. All 103 saved parameter, uncertainty, hit and
+metadata arrays match exactly between the new default and explicit `True`.
+The 27 native-truth P/F/S histograms also match the previous explicitly isolated
+build in all 102 bins including flow, raw entries and sumw2. Against explicit
+`False`, the non-smoothed arrays remain identical while 156 states change their
+smoothed q/p. This is a software regression sample, not a full-sample resolution
+measurement. The original GitHub plotting cuts are used for this regression.
